WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.540
Good morning fathers, including my brother
John.

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:07.180
This Sunday is Father's Day. It's a cultural
tradition to honor fathers, and I am going

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:11.769
to give you all a Father's Day present: A
list of tips and tricks to make your lives

00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:12.769
a little easier.

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:17.460
Here is some duct tape. We all love duct tape.
It's a very manly substance. But this is kind

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.430
of the only size it comes in, right? So if
you want a smaller piece of duct tape, you

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:24.310
have to get it off, and then you have to rip
down the side...

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:30.039
Interestingly you can actually do this permanently,
and you can do it any size at all. All you

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:33.480
need is an Exacto knife and the ability to
not cut your face of while using one.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.770
Duct tape has little strings inside of it.
You can see the little ridges where those

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:39.570
strings are. Cut in between those little strings.
You can actually have one duct tape that is,

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:44.690
in effect, devoted to several different widths
of duct tape. So just by cutting and yanking,

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:48.740
we now have a duct tape roll that has three
different widths of duct tape. So you don't

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.960
have to use the whole thing. This will make
your duct tape last much longer.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.920
Now let's talk about knots. Knots are extremely
useful. The one that we usually use is this

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:02.830
one, but it's not very good because it binds
up and it's hard to undo which is why you

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.870
should always do the figure-eight knot.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.591
Figure-eight knot: You go around, and then
back up, and through, and this is your figure-eight

00:01:08.591 --> 00:01:13.320
knot. Now that will tighten, but it's also
really easy to untighten - wink! - and it's

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.320
done.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:17.541
So all I'm doing is going around, and over,
and then back up. You can do it in a loop:

00:01:17.541 --> 00:01:22.180
go up, and then over, and around, and up with
the loop, and then you've got yourself a figure-eight

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.590
loop. And this won't go anywhere, but it's
really easy to untie so if you ever need to

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:30.350
- well - fatherhood's hard, but not that hard.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.550
And if you want to tie two strings together
- or two usb cables - with the figure-eight

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.610
knot, just do your figure-eight knot losely
with one of them, and then with the other

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:40.900
come the opposite direction and follow this
knot around.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.600
[sings, fast forwarded]

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:51.220
...do do dooo! And then you have a really
good knot that's really easy to untie.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:56.000
Tip number three: Flossing sucks. You've got
to wrap it around your fingers, and then you've

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:01.170
got to put your big ol fatherly hands all
up in your mouth, and then by the time you're

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.710
done your fingers are turning purple and they're
about to fall off.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:06.290
This is why you should get one of these. They
are inexpensive and they let you floss without

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:08.830
having to shove your fingers in your mouth.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:13.440
Number four: Do you have a bunch of old VHS
tapes and family photos lying around that

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.580
are just taking up space, and you want to
have them in a more managable format?

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:22.060
There are tons of companies on the internet
that will take your things, scan them, so

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:26.910
that you can have them in dvds or on your
computer. It's super easy, not very expensive,

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.640
and I've linked to some of them in the description
below.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.270
Disposable razors are great, but I hate it
when they start getting dull and I'm like

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:38.030
"I can do it one more week" as it yanks every
hair individually out of my face. It turns

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:42.150
out that this doesn't need to be sharpened.
What it needs to be is honed. It's not because

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:46.450
the razor is dull that it's hurting you so
much. It's because there are tiny microscopic

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:51.180
bends and imperfections that have formed in
the razor. And it's really easy to hone a

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:54.610
razor. Just take our your jeans and rub it
backwards on your jeans ten or twenty times.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.910
And all those microscopic imperfections will
totally be gone. This will be much shinier

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:03.200
and much prettier and hurt way less. This
can make expensive disposable razors last

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.010
for months instead of weeks.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:10.660
And now for my final trick, I'm going to teach
you how to relax more, eliminate pee spatter,

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:15.410
decrease marital strife, and decrease the
volume of the noice of your urination.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:19.440
Yup yup yup yup.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.120
Oh yeah, that's right. I just peed sitting
down. I know what you're thinking. You're

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.750
like "What kind of man is this?" I'll tell
you what kind of man I am. I'm a man who's

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.989
comfortable with my sexuality, and I am a
man who isn't overly concerned with irrational

00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:31.890
constructions of our society and culture.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.650
Happy Father's Day to all of the fathers.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.599
And if you are a father who is only watching
this because someone sent you the... for the

00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:40.680
tips, stop watching now because it's about
to get confusing.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:45.750
I'm playing a couple of shows in Missoula
this week and next week. July 23rd is the

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:49.239
first at the Unitarian Universalist church
with the Whomping Willows and several other

00:03:49.239 --> 00:03:52.670
wizard-rock bands. I hope that all Missoula
nerdfighters come out to those shows because

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.660
I would really like to see how many of you
there are.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:59.090
John, stop trolling! Tell us what the freaking
title of your book is, jeez! And I will see

00:03:59.090 --> 00:03:59.970
you on Monday.

